  "name": "LEUCOCYTE ADHESION DEFICIENCY (LAD I&II)",
  "code": "1514",
  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<p><strong>If LAD I is detected:</strong>Flow cytometric analysis shows&nbsp;markedly reduced or absent expression&nbsp;of CD18 and associated integrins (CD11a/CD11b) on leukocytes. This pattern is consistent with&nbsp;Leukocyte Adhesion Deficiency Type I (LAD I). The findings support a diagnosis of a &beta;2 integrin (CD18) deficiency. Clinical features such as recurrent bacterial infections, delayed umbilical cord separation, and poor wound healing are usually present. Genetic confirmation is recommended.</p>\n<p><strong>If LAD II is detected:</strong>The test shows&nbsp;markedly reduced expression of CD15s (sialyl-Lewis X)&nbsp;on neutrophils with normal CD18 and CD11a/CD11b expression. These findings are suggestive of&nbsp;Leukocyte Adhesion Deficiency Type II (LAD II). Patients often present with recurrent infections, developmental delay, and abnormal leukocyte trafficking. Molecular studies for fucosylation pathway defects are advised.</p>",
